&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in Computer Science or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of professional software engineering experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong fundamentals in data structures, algorithms, and systems-level thinking (memory management, concurrency, I/O).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in modern C++ (C++11 or higher); comfort with STL.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid working knowledge of UNIX/Linux development environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI-assisted coding tools (e.g., Claude Code, OpenCode) to accelerate development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clear, proactive communicator who works well with a globally distributed team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nice to Have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to distributed systems concepts (replication, sharding, consensus), query/compute engines, or columnar/analytical storage formats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with RPC frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
